IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-69, TARGETED: the Joint Investment Trusts Law, 5754-1994 ("the Law"). Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two references of the Law (items I1 and I2) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the individual who serves as a director or holds a post in the manager of a joint investment trust (to whom the paragraph of item I1 is addressed), and the individual who invests in a foreign fund (to whom the section of item I2 is applied). A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: a provision as the instruments read give its status, the printed words of a paragraph as a list of words, an instruction that replaces a quoted string, the two kinds of item, and the questions asked of them. No reference is stated here; they are in jt69-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
-- Section numbers are written with Latin letters for the Hebrew ones the Law uses (113ד is 113d); subsection letters are (a) alef, (b) bet.
-- THE STATUS NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A status is what the instruments READ give; the row says nothing about a provision no instrument read touches except that no instrument read touches it.
-- This row does not say which of two readings of a paragraph is the right one, what a court would do, how a provision should read, or anything about anyone's liability. It records what the pages print and what the consolidation prints.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A status in the instruments read` IS ONE OF
    `In force`
    `Amended and in force`
    Repealed

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page images, with the later instruments read and deposited (see NOTES.md)`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

-- A provision: a section or a subsection the citing words can name.
DECLARE `A provision` HAS
    `its label` IS A STRING
    `its section number` IS A NUMBER
    `its subsection` IS A STRING
    `its citation as printed` IS A STRING
    `its status in the instruments read` IS A `A status in the instruments read`
    `the instrument that changes it` IS A STRING
    `the printed date of that instrument` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the repeal began no later than` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `what the status rests on` IS A STRING

-- The printed words of one paragraph, as a list of words (the punctuation between words is not a word).
DECLARE `A printed text` HAS
    `where it is printed` IS A STRING
    `its words` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what the words were read from` IS A STRING

-- An instruction of an amending law that replaces one quoted string of a paragraph by other words.
DECLARE `An instruction that replaces a quoted string` HAS
    `where it is printed` IS A STRING
    `the paragraph it is about` IS A STRING
    `the string it replaces` IS A STRING
    `the words it puts in place` IS A LIST OF STRING

-- An instrument read: one item of an official issue, the law the issue names for it, and the paragraphs of the Law that the item names (labelled with Latin letters, as elsewhere in the row).
DECLARE `An instrument read` HAS
    `the instrument` IS A STRING
    `where it is printed` IS A STRING
    `the printed date of the issue` IS A DATE
    `the law the issue names for the item` IS A STRING
    `how the issue names the law` IS A STRING
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `what the item does` IS A STRING
    `the paragraphs of the Law it names` IS A LIST OF STRING

-- Item I1: a paragraph that cites a subsection, and an instruction that replaces the figure of the citation alone.
DECLARE `A replacement item` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words as first enacted` IS A `A printed text`
    `the instruction` IS A `An instruction that replaces a quoted string`
    `the consolidation text` IS A `A printed text`
    `the paragraph the item records` IS A STRING
    `the later instruments read` IS A LIST OF `An instrument read`
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- Item I2: one alternative of a commencement clause, kept as a period and the printed date it runs from. The row does not add the period to the date.
DECLARE `A commencement alternative` HAS
    `what it waits for` IS A STRING
    `the number of months` IS A NUMBER
    `counted from the date printed on` IS A DATE
    `where it is printed` IS A STRING

-- Item I2: a repeal whose start the instrument gives as the later of two alternatives.
DECLARE `A repeal with a deferred start` HAS
    `the instruction` IS A STRING
    `the section repealed` IS A NUMBER
    `the alternatives the clause names` IS A LIST OF `A commencement alternative`
    `the clause takes the later of the alternatives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the later alternative as a date` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `an upper bound on the day the repeal began, not a commencement date` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Item I2: a paragraph that applies a section to a foreign fund.
DECLARE `A reference to a section` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the number of the section cited` IS A NUMBER
    `the section cited` IS A `A provision`
    `the paragraph the reference records` IS A STRING
    `the printed date of the issue that prints the citing words` IS A DATE
    `the later instruments read` IS A LIST OF `An instrument read`
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- The questions. Each takes a value from jt69-cross-references.l4.

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is in force` MEANS
    (p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS `In force`) OR (p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS `Amended and in force`)

GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is repealed` MEANS p's `its status in the instruments read` EQUALS Repealed

-- In force on a day, as the instruments read give it. NOTHING when the instruments read do not settle it: a repealed provision whose start is not bounded, or a bound that is not before the day asked about.
GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the provision is in force on` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `its status in the instruments read`
        WHEN Repealed THEN
            CONSIDER p's `the repeal began no later than`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST bound THEN
                    IF Day bound LESS THAN Day d
                        THEN JUST FALSE
                        ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `In force` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Amended and in force` THEN JUST TRUE

-- The day a repeal took effect is not given by the pages this row reads (a printed date of an issue is not a day of effect), so the answer is NOTHING for every provision.
GIVEN p IS A `A provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the change to the provision took effect` MEANS NOTHING

-- A word is a section number when what comes before its first bracket reads as a number.
GIVEN token IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the word is a section number` MEANS
    CONSIDER TONUMBER (at (SPLIT token "(") 0)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST n THEN TRUE

-- Every occurrence of the word w in the list is followed by a section number. An occurrence that ends the list is followed by nothing, so it fails.
GIVEN w IS A STRING
      words IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every occurrence of the word is followed by a section number` MEANS
    CONSIDER words
        WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
        WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            (IF x EQUALS w
                THEN (CONSIDER rest
                        WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
                        WHEN y FOLLOWED BY more THEN `the word is a section number` y)
                ELSE TRUE)
            AND `every occurrence of the word is followed by a section number` w rest

-- The word that follows each occurrence of w in the list.
GIVEN w IS A STRING
      words IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the words that follow the word` MEANS
    CONSIDER words
        WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
        WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
            IF x EQUALS w
                THEN (CONSIDER rest
                        WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
                        WHEN y FOLLOWED BY more THEN y FOLLOWED BY (`the words that follow the word` w rest))
                ELSE `the words that follow the word` w rest

-- The provisions in a table that the words cite: those whose citation as printed follows an occurrence of w.
GIVEN w IS A STRING
      words IS A LIST OF STRING
      table IS A LIST OF `A provision`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A provision`
`the provisions the words cite` MEANS
    filter (GIVEN p YIELD elem (p's `its citation as printed`) (`the words that follow the word` w words)) table

GIVEN w IS A STRING
      words IS A LIST OF STRING
      table IS A LIST OF `A provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the words cite no repealed provision` MEANS
    NOT (any `the provision is repealed` (`the provisions the words cite` w words table))

-- Replace every word equal to the quoted string by the words that take its place. The row applies the instruction as written and no other rule.
GIVEN old IS A STRING
      new IS A LIST OF STRING
      words IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the words after replacing the string` MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN t YIELD IF t EQUALS old THEN new ELSE LIST t) words)

GIVEN i IS A `A replacement item`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the literal result of the instruction` MEANS
    `the words after replacing the string` (i's `the instruction`'s `the string it replaces`) (i's `the instruction`'s `the words it puts in place`) (i's `the citing words as first enacted`'s `its words`)

GIVEN p IS A STRING
      i IS A `An instrument read`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument names the paragraph` MEANS elem p (i's `the paragraphs of the Law it names`)

GIVEN p IS A STRING
      instruments IS A LIST OF `An instrument read`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some instrument in the list names the paragraph` MEANS any (GIVEN i YIELD `the instrument names the paragraph` p i) instruments

GIVEN i IS A `An instrument read`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is printed after` MEANS Day (i's `the printed date of the issue`) GREATER THAN Day d

GIVEN i IS A `A replacement item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a later instrument read touches the paragraph of the item` MEANS `some instrument in the list names the paragraph` (i's `the paragraph the item records`) (i's `the later instruments read`)

GIVEN r IS A `A reference to a section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a later instrument read touches the paragraph of the reference` MEANS `some instrument in the list names the paragraph` (r's `the paragraph the reference records`) (r's `the later instruments read`)

GIVEN i IS A `A replacement item`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs of the replacement item hold` MEANS i's `limb (a) holds` AND i's `limb (b) holds`

GIVEN r IS A `A reference to a section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs of the reference hold` MEANS r's `limb (a) holds` AND r's `limb (b) holds`

GIVEN r IS A `A reference to a section`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the section the reference cites is in force on` MEANS `the provision is in force on` (r's `the section cited`) d

GIVEN s IS A `A repeal with a deferred start`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the bound is later than a year after the printed date of every alternative` MEANS
    CONSIDER s's `an upper bound on the day the repeal began, not a commencement date`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST bound THEN
            all (GIVEN a YIELD Day bound GREATER THAN (Day (a's `counted from the date printed on`) + 366)) (s's `the alternatives the clause names`)
